  "slug": "networks-bistable-e5e6",
  "summary": "Explicit geometric domains now place multi-omic signatures and tumor architecture regimes in spaces where they can be quantified.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is the use of explicit geometric structure to place biological objects in a defined domain and quantify them there. A multi-omic signature is represented as a convex polytope in an 18-dimensional latent space, giving membership and overlap a bounded domain for assessment. A tile-based index operationalizes hyperdisorder, a proposed multiscale tumor architecture regime, across TCGA gastric cancer H&E whole-slide images. A spatially resolved atlas of gastric cancer, integrating single-cell and spatial transcriptomics, locates a lymphocyte-aggregated region that tracks T cell activation, providing molecular spatial context. The items differ in modality, scale, and application, so the shared element is methodological rather than topical. What is new is the commitment to a bounded or structured domain in which each object is located and measured, with quantitative claims tied to the stated examples.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-01-31"
}
